#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
ansi2irc — bidirectional converter between IRC and ANSI

Features:
- Converts irc2ansi and ansi2irc (auto-detect or explicit via --direction)
- Builds fast lookup tables between IRC99 and ANSI256 palettes; caches them
- Nearest-colour search separates chroma from luma: chromatic→chromatic, grayscale→grayscale
- Streams: reads from STDIN and writes to STDOUT
- Virtual Terminal implementation for proper cursor handling in ansi2irc

Notes:
- IRC control bytes used: Color ^C (0x03), Bold ^B (0x02), Underline ^_ (0x1F),
  Reverse ^V (0x16), Italic ^] (0x1D), Reset ^O (0x0F)
- ANSI SGR handled: 0 reset, 1 bold, 3 italic, 4 underline, 7 reverse,
  22/23/24/27 attribute off, 30-37/90-97 fg, 40-47/100-107 bg,
  38/48 256-colour (5;n) and truecolor (2;r;g;b)
"""
